  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "simplifyStatement",
    "file": "skia/src/sksl/SkSLCompiler.cpp",
    "description": "Constant-if folding replaces an IfStatement with its selected branch or a Nop (lines 1352-1367) but discards the returned old statement instead of retaining it in OptimizationContext::fOwnedStatements. Destroying the eliminated branch destroys its VarDeclaration while the symbol-table-owned Variable survives with fDeclaration still pointing at that freed declaration. A later VariableReference::constantPropagate calls Variable::initialValue(), which dereferences the dangling fDeclaration and causes the use-after-poison. This is the same lifetime issue that the dead-variable-declaration path at lines 1342-1347 explicitly avoids.",
    "conditions": "Provide SkSL in which a condition becomes a BoolLiteral during optimization, an eliminated if branch contains a local variable declaration, and a surviving VariableReference resolves to that variable. In the PoC `void a(){if(2>2)int a;a;}`, `2>2` folds to false; simplifyStatement replaces the no-else if with Nop, freeing `int a`, while the final `a;` retains the Variable pointer. After CFG rescan, constant propagation queries that variable's initial value through the stale VarDeclaration pointer and crashes."
  },
